<file path="README.md">
# 🛡️ CypherMind — Self-Learning AI Penetration Testing Copilot

A local, multi-agent AI penetration testing framework with Q-learning orchestration, hybrid RAG, taint analysis, and Red vs Blue self-play.

## Quick Start

```bash
cd ~/cyphermind
bash scripts/install.sh
bash scripts/start.sh
```

Open **http://localhost:3000**

**Documentation:**
- [Project Overview & Architecture](docs/PROJECT_OVERVIEW.md) — full system summary, how to run, API reference
- [Fine-Tuning Guide](docs/FINE_TUNING_GUIDE.md) — step-by-step fine-tuning workflow

## Architecture

| Tier | Component |
|------|-----------|
| 1 | Q-Learning agent orchestrator (ε-greedy) |
| 2 | Multi-agent swarm: Recon, SAST, Exploit, PostExploit |
| 3 | Hybrid RAG: ChromaDB + BM25 + cross-encoder |
| 4 | Taint analysis graph (NetworkX) |
| 5 | Self-play Red vs Blue arena |
| 6 | Bradley-Terry preference learning |
| 7 | Real-time WebSocket event streaming |

## Manual Start

```bash
# Terminal 1 — Backend
cd backend && source .venv/bin/activate
export PYTHONPATH=.
uvicorn app.main:app --reload --port 8000

# Terminal 2 — Frontend
cd frontend && npm run dev
```

## LLM Providers (NVIDIA, Grok, OpenAI, …)

All LLM calls go through `backend/app/llm/` — **change provider in `.env` only**, no code edits.

### Quick setup — Kimi for bug bounty, Grok for self-play

```bash
# Default provider
LLM_DEFAULT_PROVIDER=nvidia

# API keys
NVIDIA_API_KEY=your_nvidia_key
GROK_API_KEY=your_xai_key

# Per-task routing
LLM_PROVIDER_BUG_BOUNTY=nvidia      # Kimi via NVIDIA NIM
LLM_PROVIDER_SELFPLAY=grok          # Grok for red/blue arena
LLM_PROVIDER_SELFPLAY_RED=grok
LLM_PROVIDER_SELFPLAY_BLUE=nvidia
LLM_PROVIDER_RAG=nvidia
LLM_PROVIDER_CHAT=grok
```

### Available provider presets

| Name | API | Default model |
|------|-----|---------------|
| `nvidia` / `kimi` | integrate.api.nvidia.com | moonshotai/kimi-k2.6 |
| `grok` | api.x.ai | grok-2-latest |
| `openai` | api.openai.com | gpt-4o |
| `openrouter` | openrouter.ai | claude-sonnet-4 |
| `custom` | your URL | llama3 |

Env vars per provider: `{PROVIDER}_API_KEY`, `{PROVIDER}_API_BASE`, `{PROVIDER}_MODEL`  
Or prefixed: `LLM_GROK_API_KEY`, `LLM_GROK_MODEL`, etc.

### API

- `GET /api/v1/settings/llm-providers/list` — all presets + role mappings
- `GET /api/v1/settings/llm` — health check default provider
- `GET /api/v1/settings/llm/grok` — health check specific provider

### Architecture

```
app/llm/
  base.py          — presets + ProviderConfig
  registry.py      — resolve name/role → provider
  openai_compat.py — OpenAI-compatible HTTP client
  facade.py        — chat_completion_raw(), chat_completion()
app/services/llm_service.py  — thin re-export (backward compat)
```

## LLM (NVIDIA API — legacy section)

CypherMind uses **OpenAI-compatible APIs**. Default is NVIDIA NIM with `moonshotai/kimi-k2.6`.

Optional Google Custom Search (falls back to DuckDuckGo if unset):

```bash
GOOGLE_API_KEY=your_google_api_key
GOOGLE_CSE_ID=your_search_engine_id
```

## Autonomous Bug Bounty (Cybernote 2026 Methodology)

LLM-driven **BugBountyAgent** with **30+ tools** implementing the full 13-phase bug bounty workflow:

| Phase | Capability |
|-------|------------|
| 1 | Passive subdomain enum (crt.sh, subfinder, chaos) |
| 2 | DNS bruteforce & ffuf subdomain fuzz |
| 3 | ASN / infrastructure mapping |
| 4–5 | Alive host detection (httpx) |
| 6 | VHOST enumeration |
| 7 | URL discovery (wayback, katana, gau) |
| 8 | JS secret extraction |
| 9 | Directory & sensitive file fuzz |
| 10 | GitHub recon |
| 11–12 | Port scan + nuclei |
| 13 | Subdomain takeover |

- **UI:** http://localhost:3000/bug-bounty
- **API:** `POST /api/v1/bug-bounty/hunt` — `{ "target_url": "https://...", "pipeline_mode": "full" }`
- **Methodology:** `GET /api/v1/bug-bounty/methodology`
- **Wordlists:** `GET /api/v1/wordlists/status` — upload via UI or `POST /api/v1/wordlists/upload/dns`

### Wordlists & API keys (`.env`)

```bash
DNS_WORDLIST=/usr/share/seclists/Discovery/DNS/subdomains-top1million-110000.txt
WEB_WORDLIST=/usr/share/seclists/Discovery/Web-Content/common.txt
PARAMS_WORDLIST=/usr/share/seclists/Discovery/Web-Content/burp-parameter-names.txt
GITHUB_TOKEN=ghp_...          # Phase 10 GitHub recon
PDCP_API_KEY=...              # ProjectDiscovery Chaos (Phase 1)
RUN_METHODOLOGY_ON_HUNT=true  # Auto-run pipeline before LLM
METHODOLOGY_PIPELINE_MODE=default  # or "full" for all 13 phases
```

Bundled fallbacks live in `data/wordlists/` — see `data/wordlists/README.md`.

RAG enrichment: use `enrich_finding_with_rag` tool or ingest `data/knowledge/bug_bounty_methodology.md` into the knowledge base.

## Continuous Learning (No Fine-Tuning)

CypherMind gets smarter over time **without retraining the LLM**:

| System | What it learns | Persists to |
|--------|----------------|-------------|
| **Attack Memory** | Findings, payloads, tool sequences | SQLite + RAG |
| **Self-play → RAG** | Novel red-team attack patterns | Auto-ingested after each game |
| **Phase Q-Learning** | Best methodology phases per target type | `data/phase_q_table.json` |
| **Agent Q-Learning** | Best agent combos (Recon/SAST/Exploit/Post) | `data/q_table.json` |
| **Bradley-Terry** | Human preference on agent combos | Influences orchestrator selection |

**API:** `GET /api/v1/learning/summary` — unified learning stats

Each bug bounty hunt now:
1. **Loads** past attack patterns into the agent prompt
2. **Runs** Q-learned methodology phases (not static defaults)
3. **Stores** findings + successful tool chains for next hunt
4. **Updates** phase Q-values based on what produced results

New tool: `search_attack_memory` — agent can query learned patterns mid-hunt.

## Fine-Tuning (Optional, Separate Module)

Fine-tuning is **fully separate** from continuous learning and **disabled by default**. When disabled, all roles use your normal providers (Kimi, Grok, NVIDIA, etc.). When enabled, configured roles route to your fine-tuned model ID.

### Workflow

1. **Run hunts** — findings, attack memory, and self-play accumulate training data
2. **Build dataset** — `POST /api/v1/finetuning/build-dataset`
3. **Train externally** — upload the JSONL to your provider's fine-tuning console (OpenAI, NVIDIA, etc.)
4. **Set model ID** — `FINETUNING_MODEL_ID=ft:...` in `.env` or `POST /api/v1/finetuning/config`
5. **Enable** — `POST /api/v1/finetuning/toggle {"enabled": true}` or `FINETUNING_ENABLED=true`
6. **Disable anytime** — toggle off to fall back to base models instantly

### `.env` options

```bash
FINETUNING_ENABLED=false              # master switch (default off)
FINETUNING_MODEL_ID=ft:your-model-id  # your trained model
FINETUNING_BASE_PROVIDER=nvidia       # inherits API base/key from this preset
FINETUNING_ROLES=bug_bounty,agent     # which roles use the fine-tuned model
FINETUNING_AUTO_EXPORT=false          # auto-export JSONL after each hunt
FINETUNING_SUPPORTS_TOOLS=true
```

### API

| Endpoint | Purpose |
|----------|---------|
| `GET /api/v1/finetuning/status` | Module status, roles, datasets |
| `POST /api/v1/finetuning/toggle` | Enable/disable at runtime |
| `POST /api/v1/finetuning/config` | Update model ID, roles, base provider |
| `POST /api/v1/finetuning/build-dataset` | Export training JSONL |
| `GET /api/v1/finetuning/health` | Test fine-tuned model connectivity |

Runtime state persists in `data/finetuning/runtime_state.json` — toggling via API survives restarts.

## API

- `GET /health` — health check
- `GET /api/v1/dashboard/stats` — dashboard metrics
- `POST /api/v1/engagements` — create engagement
- `POST /api/v1/agents/execute` — run agents (RL or manual)
- `WS /ws/engagements/{id}` — live agent events
- `POST /api/v1/knowledge/query` — hybrid RAG search
- `POST /api/v1/selfplay/start` — Red vs Blue arena

Full docs: http://localhost:8000/docs

## Tests

```bash
cd backend && source .venv/bin/activate
export PYTHONPATH=.
pytest ../tests -v
```

## Sample Vulnerable Code

Test SAST/taint analysis with `data/samples/vulnerable_app.py`
